  "Specification": "This module, MCEWD687a, is a model-checking harness for the EWD687a leader election protocol. It defines model values for processes and edges, and encodes a postcondition that describes a counterexample trace as a sequence of states and actions, likely for use in debugging or validation. The module asserts a temporal property LeaderPermanentlyActive, which requires that eventually, always, the Terminated predicate holds over the system variables. The module also includes a constraint constr_1633116534008313000 that bounds the values of message and acknowledgment counters, as well as unacknowledged messages, for all edges. All protocol logic and variable declarations are inherited from the EWD687a module, and this module serves primarily as a configuration and property-checking wrapper for model checking.",
